# Media-index working data (scripts/media-index/ output).
# Never commit this tree — this repo is PUBLIC and the tree contains:
#   - Dropbox share URLs with live `rlkey` access tokens for Miles's client
#     deliverables (103 occurrences at last count)
#   - copies of client brand-guide PDFs
#   - extracted keyframes of identifiable people (model-release status unknown)
# It's also ~92 MB of derived output that's reproducible from the scripts.
# Leading slash matters: an unanchored `media-index/` would also swallow
# `scripts/media-index/`, which is the tooling and does belong in the repo.
#
# This is an allowlist, not a denylist: everything under /media-index/ is
# ignored, then a few specific credential-free records are re-included below.
# A new file added to that tree stays ignored unless it is named here.
/media-index/**
# Re-include directories so git can descend to the allowed files.
!/media-index/**/
# Shot records: the durable output of the vision pass — timecodes plus
# descriptions, the thing that actually feeds the issue #15 reel. Personal
# names are redacted; see scripts/media-index/README.md.
!/media-index/data/assets/*/shots.json
!/media-index/data/shots-summary.json
# Brand-guide synthesis (not the source PDFs, which are client property).
!/media-index/data/documents/*/synthesis.json
